<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>Enums on Beyond Swift</title><link>https://beyondswift.com/tags/enums/</link><description>Recent content in Enums on Beyond Swift</description><generator>Hugo -- 0.163.3</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 12 May 2025 10:42:00 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://beyondswift.com/tags/enums/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>How big is an enum with associated values?</title><link>https://beyondswift.com/associated-values-in-enums/</link><pubDate>Mon, 12 May 2025 10:42:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://beyondswift.com/associated-values-in-enums/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Here is a four-case enum for an image cell, the kind that ships in every feed. Right now the value is in the &lt;code&gt;.idle&lt;/code&gt; case, holding nothing at all. How many bytes does that empty value occupy?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;Bitmap&lt;/span&gt; { &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// 64 bytes, stored inline&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; pixels: (UInt64, UInt64, UInt64, UInt64,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; UInt64, UInt64, UInt64, UInt64)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;enum&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;ImageState&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; idle
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; loading(progress: Double) &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// 8 bytes&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; ready(Bitmap) &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// 64 bytes&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; failed(code: Int) &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// 8 bytes&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Most people answer &amp;ldquo;a few bytes, it&amp;rsquo;s empty.&amp;rdquo; The real answer is 72. By the end you will know why an idle enum carries the weight of its heaviest sibling, and the one keyword that cuts it back down.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>